    "result_text": "The mapper correctly maps `birthDate` both directions (line 78/105 for `toOwner`, line 40 for response) and computes `ageBand` (line 56). \n\nAll changes are complete and the full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Change: derive `ageBand` from `birthDate`\n\nThe request may now include an optional ISO `birthDate`; when present, the owner response carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against `registrationDate`.\n\n**Where each piece lives (single responsibility, reusing existing patterns):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and `ageBand` (read-only string enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec, so this drives the generated `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` and `birthDate` field.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so a birth date supplied on `POST` survives to the later `GET`.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`util/AgeBand`** \u2014 a small, focused helper (alongside `BusinessDay`, `CustomerCode`, `Luhn`) that computes the band label from a birth date and a reference date using completed years.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `toOwner` maps `birthDate` by name automatically (so `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` persist it with no new pipeline step), and a new `ageBand(owner)` expression maps `AgeBand.of(birthDate, registrationDate)` to the DTO enum, returning `null` when no birth date was supplied \u2014 mirroring how the other derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, \u2026) are computed in one place.\n\nNo new function classes or YAML steps were needed: birth date flows through the existing build/save/respond pipeline, and the age band is a pure derivation belonging in the mapper.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`, birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass (1 test, 0 failures).",
